{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795089294,"nonce":"gD34ejuLoWUFwarPJn6wHE/UlCs=","message":"Implemented the installed Haxe KnowledgeGraph facade and a normal native hxn-assets package; the engine is included, while annotations/publication opt in to projection. Internal scalar and JIT producer crates create variants of one haxelib. The CLI supports hxn assets build --jit|--no-jit and direct Haxe uses hxn_assets_jit=on|off|auto. Portable checkpoints use hxn-file, including IndexedDB. Real installed consumers pass on macOS Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp/CPPIA, Ash wasm and both Emscripten modes with Rust tooling disabled; scalar/JIT checkpoints interchange. Simulator/emulator graph and fresh-process persistence checks pass for iOS Ash/hxcpp and Android scalar/JIT on both runtimes. Linux NUC repeats shared-inbox and scalar/JIT backend concurrency checks. Emscripten graph parsing requires a larger native stack: KnowledgeGraph now supplies 8 MiB, overrideable via hxn_assets_stack_size. Matching file/asset archives built from the shared lock/toolchain compose in threaded Emscripten. Fixed the core shared-outbox issue separately (hxn 2b87e5e); core 0.3.10 CI is green and tag publication is running before pinning and releasing this workspace as 0.2.0. KyuGraph source support is merged to main at 64f41a2 at the user’s request. Native notices moved from the old separate adapter inventory into hxn-assets; hxn-file retains only its own dependency inventory.","files":null}]}